evanwang  staff     128 Aug 17 15:50 traces\n-rw-r--r--@  1 evanwang  staff   14275 Aug 17 15:23 verify.py\nYou are refactoring one Lean 4 proof for the Lean Refactor Arena.\n\n## Target\n\n- Theorem: `{name}`\n- Corpus: {source}\n- Work file (edit this file, nothing else): `{work_file}`\n- Lean project root: `{project_dir}` (toolchain {primary_version})\n- Must also compile unchanged on: {other_versions}\n\nThe work file is the prefix of the upstream source file (imports, `open`s,\n`variable`s, section context) followed by the target declaration with its\noriginal proof. Everything above the declaration is context: do not touch it.\nScoring re-splices your declaration into the pristine upstream file, so any edit\nyou make above the declaration is discarded — only the declaration counts.\n\n## Official objective\n\nMaximize the arena leaderboard score, not length or heartbeats separately:\n\n`combined = (length_reduction_pct + heartbeat_reduction_pct + survival_pct) / 3`\n\nFull survival on every listed toolchain is a hard constraint. Once survival is\n100%, rank candidates by:\n\n`objective_sum_pct = length_reduction_pct + heartbeat_reduction_pct`\n\nThis is a real tradeoff. A longer proof is better when its heartbeat gain is\nlarger than its length loss. Likewise, do not over-golf tokens if that makes\nelaboration sufficiently more expensive. Compare the sum printed by `check`.\n\nReferences: {ref_heartbeats} heartbeats and {ref_length} proof tokens.\n\nPrefer compact constructor/term proofs and explicit stable lemmas. Avoid broad\nautomation (`simp` without a lemma list, `aesop`, `grind`, large `omega`) when\nit burns more heartbeats than the token reduction is worth. Measure rather\nthan guessing.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- The statement must stay **byte-identical**, including binders and\n  implicit/instance arguments. Only the proof after `:=` may change.\n- The submission is *the statement plus one proof, nothing else*. Do **not**\n  add any top-level declaration: no `lemma`/`theorem` helpers, no `def`,\n  `abbrev`, `instance`, `structure`, `inductive`, `class`, `opaque`,\n  `attribute`, `macro`, `notation`, `syntax`, `deriving instance`, and no new\n  top-level `set_option ... in` / `open ... in` beyond whatever the statement\n  already carries. Factor shared work into `have`/`let`/`suffices` **inside**\n  the proof.\n- Forbidden anywhere in the proof: `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide`,\n  `ofReduceBool`, `ofReduceNat`, `#eval`, `#reduce`, `#exit`, `IO.*`,\n  `unsafe`, `extern`, `initialize`, `run_cmd`, `run_elab`,\n  `#count_heartbeats`, `@[implemented_by]`, `@[extern]`.\n- Do not edit any other file, do not edit anything under `.lake/`, and do not\n  change the project's toolchain or dependencies.\n\n## Optional notes\n\nThe long local playbook is in `{competition_dir}/STRATEGY.md`; syntax and\nversion notes are in `LEAN_SYNTAX.md` and `VERSION_MATRIX.md`. Open a relevant\nsection only when blocked. Corpus/theorem search is usually more useful than\nreading these files front to back.\n\n## How to check your work\n\nRun from `{competition_dir}` **only**. Do not run `lake`, `lean`, or\n`lake env lean` — `check` already compiles the proof and prints errors.\n\n```\npython3 arena.py check --name \"{name}\"                # newest toolchain only (fast)\npython3 arena.py check --name \"{name}\" --all-versions # full robustness + score\n```\n\n`check` is the only scorer and the only compiler. Use `rg`/`sed` on the\ncorpus under `.lake/packages` to find lemmas. Do not use Lean MCP tools.\n\nLoop:\n\n1. Maintain an incumbent among compiling candidates: highest\n   `objective_sum_pct` wins. Preserve its proof before trying another edit.\n2. Use at most **10** fast checks. Never re-check an unchanged proof.\n3. After finding the first candidate with positive `objective_sum_pct`, try at\n   least two and at most four additional **distinct** simplifications. Stop\n   early after two consecutive checks fail to improve the incumbent.\n4. Restore the incumbent and run one `--all-versions`.\n5. If every listed version passes, stop immediately. If compatibility fails,\n   make only compatibility-directed repairs, using at most two further fast\n   checks before repeating `--all-versions`.\n\nDo not require both reduction components to be positive; only their sum and\nfull survival determine whether a trade improves the leaderboard.\n\n## When you are done\n\nLeave the final proof in the work file (last declaration in the file). Reply\nwith: what you changed, the final length and heartbeats versus the\nreference, which toolchains pass, and any rewrite that did not work.\n5:  arena.py check   --name N        extract, compile, measure, score\n6:  arena.py run     --name N        prepare → run Codex → check → record episode\n9:`check` is what the agent calls while it works; `run` is the outer loop that\n15:import argparse\n18:import subprocess\n36:WRAPPER_ID = \"v3-official-objective\"\n99:def check(\n120:    published_hb = local_score.original_heartbeats(name) or 0\n122:    ref_hb = local_ref.get(\"heartbeats\") or published_hb\n124:    hb = res[\"heartbeats\"]\n140:    survival_pct = (\n145:    objective_sum = (\n150:    combined_pct = (\n151:        round((objective_sum + survival_pct) / 3, 2)\n152:        if objective_sum is not None\n162:        \"heartbeats\": hb,\n163:        \"reference_heartbeats\": ref_hb,\n164:        \"heartbeat_reduction_pct\": hb_pct,\n165:        \"objective_sum_pct\": objective_sum,\n166:        \"survival_pct\": survival_pct,\n167:        \"combined_pct\": combined_pct,\n177:        out[\"published_heartbeats\"] = published_hb\n189:    ref_hb = local_ref.get(\"heartbeats\") or local_score.original_heartbeats(name)\n197:        ref_heartbeats=ref_hb,\n207:        \"--skip-git-repo-check\",\n223:    info: dict[str, Any] = {\"model\": model, \"effort\": effort, \"wrapper\": WRAPPER_ID}\n225:        proc = subprocess.Popen(\n226:            cmd, cwd=ROOT, stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n227:            stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True,\n268:def run_episode(\n285:        \"heartbeats\": ref.get(\"heartbeats\") or local_score.original_heartbeats(name),\n291:    after = check(name, all_versions=True, timeout=timeout)\n297:        \"wrapper\": WRAPPER_ID,\n326:            f\"hb_local={ref.get('heartbeats')} hb_published={ref.get('published_heartbeats')}\"\n331:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n339:    c = sub.add_parser(\"check\")\n363:    elif args.cmd == \"check\":\n364:        print(json.dumps(check(args.name, all_versions=args.all_versions,\n369:        rec = run_episode(args.name, model=args.model, effort=args.effort,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,420p' arena.py\nfind runs -maxdepth 1 -type d -name '2026082*' -print | sort\njq -r 'select(.name==\\\"CallElimCorrect.extractedOldExprInVars\\\" or .name==\\\"Cslib.SKI.parallelReduction_diamond\\\" or .name==\\\"Core.InitsUpdatesComm\\\" or .name==\\\"interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps\\\") | [.timestamp,.wrapper,.name,.run_dir,.score.length_reduction_pct,.score.heartbeat_reduction_pct,.score.objective_sum_pct,.score.survival_pct] | @tsv' runs/episodes.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,420p' arena.py\nfind runs -maxdepth 1 -type d -name '2026082*' -print | sort\njq -r 'select(.name==\\\"CallElimCorrect.extractedOldExprInVars\\\" or .name==\\\"Cslib.SKI.parallelReduction_diamond\\\" or .name==\\\"Core.InitsUpdatesComm\\\" or .name==\\\"interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps\\\") | [.timestamp,.wrapper,.name,.run_dir,.score.length_reduction_pct,.score.heartbeat_reduction_pct,.score.objective_sum_pct,.score.survival_pct] | @tsv' runs/episodes.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Episode harness for the Lean Refactor Arena.\n\n  arena.py prepare --name N        materialise the work file inside its project\n  arena.py check   --name N        extract, compile, measure, score\n  arena.py run     --name N        prepare → run Codex → check → record episode\n  arena.py list                    problems, toolchains, local readiness\n\n`check` is what the agent calls while it works; `run` is the outer loop that\nproduces a trace + JSONL episode record.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nimport local_score\nimport verify\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nRUNS = ROOT / \"runs\"\nPROMPT = ROOT / \"prompts\" / \"refactor.md\"\nEPISODES = RUNS / \"episodes.jsonl\"\n\nDEFAULT_MODEL = \"gpt-5.6-sol\"\nDEFAULT_EFFORT = \"max\"  # `ultra` also exists but delegates subtasks\n# Prompt + tool profile id; bump when iterating the wrapper.\nWRAPPER_ID = \"v3-official-objective\"\n\n\ndef slug(name: str) -> str:\n    return re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9]+\", \"_\", name).strip(\"_\")\n\n\ndef primary_version(name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    return verify.newest_version(verify.versions_for(name))\n\n\ndef work_file(name: str, version: Optional[str] = None) -> Optional[Path]:\n    version = version or primary_version(name)\n    proj = verify.project_dir(version) if version else None\n    return proj / \"Arena\" / f\"{slug(name)}.lean\" if proj else None\n\n\ndef local_reference() -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Reference measurements taken with *our* method (see verify.py).\"\"\"\n    return verify.read_references()\n\n\ndef prepare(name: str, version: Optional[str] = None, *, force: bool = False) -> Path:\n    row = verify.BENCHMARK[name]\n    version = version or primary_version(name)\n    proj = verify.project_dir(version)\n    if proj is None:\n        sys.exit(f\"no local project for {version}\")\n    dest = work_file(name, version)\n    assert dest is not None\n    if dest.exists() and not force:\n        return dest\n\n    rel = row.get(\"file_path\")\n    if rel:\n        src_file = verify.find_source_file(proj, rel)\n        if src_file is None:\n            sys.exit(f\"source file not found in {proj}: {rel}\")\n        text = src_file.read_text()\n        start = verify.decl_start(text, row)\n        if start is None:\n            sys.exit(\"could not locate declaration in source file\")\n        prefix = verify.trim_decl_modifiers(text[:start])\n        body = f\"{prefix}\\n{row['src'].rstrip()}\\n\"\n    else:\n        body = f\"{row.get('header', '')}\\n{row['src'].rstrip()}\\n\"\n\n    dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    dest.write_text(body)\n    return dest\n\n\ndef extract_candidate(name: str, version: Optional[str] = None) -> Optional[str]:\n    path = work_file(name, version)\n    if path is None or not path.exists():\n        return None\n    text = path.read_text()\n    start = verify.decl_start(text, verify.BENCHMARK[name])\n    if start is None:\n        return None\n    return text[start:].strip()\n\n\ndef check(\n    name: str,\n    *,\n    all_versions: bool = False,\n    timeout: int = 1800,\n    candidate: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    row = verify.BENCHMARK[name]\n    if candidate is None:\n        candidate = extract_candidate(name)\n    if not candidate:\n        return {\"name\": name, \"error\": \"no work file — run `arena.py prepare` first\"}\n\n    versions = verify.versions_for(name)\n    if not all_versions:\n        top = primary_version(name)\n        versions = [top] if top else []\n\n    res = verify.verify(name, candidate, versions=versions, timeout=timeout)\n    length = local_score.proof_length(candidate, row[\"statement\"], name=name)\n    ref_len = local_score.original_length(name) or 0\n    published_hb = local_score.original_heartbeats(name) or 0\n    local_ref = local_reference().get(name, {})\n    ref_hb = local_ref.get(\"heartbeats\") or published_hb\n\n    hb = res[\"heartbeats\"]\n    forbidden = local_score.forbidden_hit(candidate)\n    extra = [f\"{kind} {n}\" for kind, n in local_score.count_toplevel_decls(candidate)\n             if n != name and n.split(\".\")[-1] != name.split(\".\")[-1]]\n\n    len_pct = (\n        round((ref_len - length) / ref_len * 100, 2)\n        if (ref_len and length is not None)\n        else None\n    )\n    hb_pct = (\n        round((ref_hb - hb) / ref_hb * 100, 2)\n        if (ref_hb and hb)\n        else None\n    )\n    compat = res[\"compat\"]\n    survival_pct = (\n        round(sum(bool(ok) for ok in compat.values()) / len(compat) * 100, 2)\n        if compat\n        else 0.0\n    )\n    objective_sum = (\n        round(len_pct + hb_pct, 2)\n        if len_pct is not None and hb_pct is not None\n        else None\n    )\n    combined_pct = (\n        round((objective_sum + survival_pct) / 3, 2)\n        if objective_sum is not None\n        else None\n    )\n\n    out: dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"name\": name,\n        \"compiled\": res[\"compiled\"],\n        \"length\": length,\n        \"reference_length\": ref_len,\n        \"length_reduction_pct\": len_pct,\n        \"heartbeats\": hb,\n        \"reference_heartbeats\": ref_hb,\n        \"heartbeat_reduction_pct\": hb_pct,\n        \"objective_sum_pct\": objective_sum,\n        \"survival_pct\": survival_pct,\n        \"combined_pct\": combined_pct,\n        \"compat\": compat,\n        \"statement_ok\": local_score.statements_match(row[\"statement\"], candidate, name=name),\n        \"per_version\": res[\"per_version\"],\n    }\n    if forbidden:\n        out[\"forbidden\"] = forbidden\n    if extra:\n        out[\"extra_toplevel_decls\"] = extra\n    if published_hb and ref_hb != published_hb:\n        out[\"published_heartbeats\"] = published_hb\n    return out\n\n\n# ── Codex episode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef build_prompt(name: str) -> str:\n    row = verify.BENCHMARK[name]\n    versions = verify.versions_for(name)\n    top = primary_version(name)\n    others = [v for v in versions if v != top]\n    local_ref = local_reference().get(name, {})\n    ref_hb = local_ref.get(\"heartbeats\") or local_score.original_heartbeats(name)\n    return PROMPT.read_text().format(\n        name=name,\n        source=row.get(\"source\", \"?\"),\n        work_file=str(work_file(name)),\n        project_dir=str(verify.project_dir(top)),\n        primary_version=top,\n        other_versions=\", \".join(others) if others else \"(none — single toolchain)\",\n        ref_heartbeats=ref_hb,\n        ref_length=local_score.original_length(name),\n        competition_dir=str(ROOT),\n    )\n\n\ndef codex_command(name: str, model: str, effort: str) -> list[str]:\n    return [\n        \"codex\", \"exec\",\n        \"--ignore-user-config\",           # thin, reproducible tool profile\n        \"--skip-git-repo-check\",\n        \"-C\", str(ROOT),\n        \"-s\", \"workspace-write\",\n        \"-m\", model,\n        \"-c\", f'model_reasoning_effort=\"{effort}\"',\n        \"--json\",\n    ]\n\n\nSESSION_KEYS = (\"session_id\", \"conversation_id\", \"thread_id\", \"rollout_path\")\n\n\ndef run_codex(name: str, model: str, effort: str, log_path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    cmd = codex_command(name, model, effort)\n    prompt = build_prompt(name)\n    started = time.time()\n    info: dict[str, Any] = {\"model\": model, \"effort\": effort, \"wrapper\": WRAPPER_ID}\n    with log_path.open(\"w\") as log:\n        proc = subprocess.Popen(\n            cmd, cwd=ROOT, stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n            stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True,\n        )\n        assert proc.stdin and proc.stdout\n        proc.stdin.write(prompt)\n        proc.stdin.close()\n        for line in proc.stdout:\n            log.write(line)\n            log.flush()\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n                continue\n            try:\n                event = json.loads(line)\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                continue\n            for key in SESSION_KEYS:\n                found = _deep_get(event, key)\n                if found and key not in info:\n                    info[key] = found\n        proc.wait()\n    info[\"exit_code\"] = proc.returncode\n    info[\"wall_seconds\"] = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n    return info\n\n\ndef _deep_get(obj: Any, key: str) -> Optional[Any]:\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        if isinstance(obj.get(key), str):\n            return obj[key]\n        for value in obj.values():\n            found = _deep_get(value, key)\n            if found:\n                return found\n    elif isinstance(obj, list):\n        for value in obj:\n            found = _deep_get(value, key)\n            if found:\n                return found\n    return None\n\n\ndef run_episode(\n    name: str,\n    *,\n    model: str = DEFAULT_MODEL,\n    effort: str = DEFAULT_EFFORT,\n    timeout: int = 1800,\n    fresh: bool = True,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    stamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\")\n    run_dir = RUNS / f\"{stamp}-{slug(name)}\"\n    run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    wf = prepare(name, force=fresh)\n    (run_dir / \"before.lean\").write_text(wf.read_text())\n    ref = local_reference().get(name, {})\n    before = {\n        \"length\": local_score.original_length(name),\n        \"heartbeats\": ref.get(\"heartbeats\") or local_score.original_heartbeats(name),\n        \"compiled\": ref.get(\"compiled\"),\n    }\n\n    codex_info = run_codex(name, model, effort, run_dir / \"codex.jsonl\")\n\n    after = check(name, all_versions=True, timeout=timeout)\n    (run_dir / \"after.lean\").write_text(wf.read_text())\n\n    record = {\n        \"timestamp\": stamp,\n        \"name\": name,\n        \"wrapper\": WRAPPER_ID,\n        \"run_dir\": str(run_dir),\n        \"codex\": codex_info,\n        \"before\": before,\n        \"after\": after,\n        \"candidate\": extract_candidate(name),\n    }\n    EPISODES.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with EPISODES.open(\"a\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(record) + \"\\n\")\n    (run_dir / \"episode.json\").write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2))\n    return record\n\n\n# ── Readiness ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef list_problems() -> None:\n    refs = local_reference()\n    for name in verify.BENCHMARK:\n        versions = verify.versions_for(name)\n        top = primary_version(name)\n        ref = refs.get(name, {})\n        compat = ref.get(\"compat\") or {}\n        ready = \"\".join(\".\" if compat.get(v) else \"x\" for v in versions) or \"?\"\n        print(\n            f\"{name}\\n\"\n            f\"    corpus={verify.BENCHMARK[name].get('source')} primary={top} \"\n            f\"versions={','.join(versions)} env={ready} \"\n            f\"len={local_score.original_length(name)} \"\n            f\"hb_local={ref.get('heartbeats')} hb_published={ref.get('published_heartbeats')}\"\n        )\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n    p = sub.add_parser(\"prepare\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n    p.add_argument(\"--version\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"reset to the reference proof\")\n\n    c = sub.add_parser(\"check\")\n    c.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n    c.add_argument(\"--all-versions\", action=\"store_true\")\n    c.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=1800)\n\n    r = sub.add_parser(\"run\")\n    r.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n    r.add_argument(\"--model\", default=DEFAULT_MODEL)\n    r.add_argument(\"--effort\", default=DEFAULT_EFFORT)\n    r.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=1800)\n    r.add_argument(\"--keep-work-file\", action=\"store_true\",\n                   help=\"continue from the current work file instead of resetting\")\n\n    sub.add_parser(\"list\")\n\n    pr = sub.add_parser(\"prompt\")\n    pr.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    if getattr(args, \"name\", None) and args.name not in verify.BENCHMARK:\n        sys.exit(f\"unknown problem: {args.name}\")\n\n    if args.cmd == \"prepare\":\n        print(prepare(args.name, args.version, force=args.force))\n    elif args.cmd == \"check\":\n        print(json.dumps(check(args.name, all_versions=args.all_versions,\n                               timeout=args.timeout), indent=2))\n    elif args.cmd == \"prompt\":\n        print(build_prompt(args.name))\n    elif args.cmd == \"run\":\n        rec = run_episode(args.name, model=args.model, effort=args.effort,\n                          timeout=args.timeout, fresh=not args.keep_work_file)\n        print(json.dumps(rec[\"after\"], indent=2))\n    elif args.cmd == \"list\":\n        list_problems()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nruns/20260820T224127Z-Cslib_SKI_parallelReduction_diamond\nruns/20260820T224711Z-CallElimCorrect_extractedOldExprInVars\