cost and length; I’m moving to the required three-toolchain robustness sweep now.\nThe full robustness sweep passes unchanged on v4.31.0, v4.30.0, and v4.29.0. Final measured candidate: 620 tokens and 5,109 heartbeats on the scoring toolchain, versus 1,353 and 10,119. I’m doing a final scope/diff check to confirm only the requested proof file changed and the declaration remains the file’s final content.\nRefactored the proof in [interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps.lean](/Users/evanwang/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.31/Arena/interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps.lean).  - Length: **620** vs. 1353 — 54.18% reduction - Heartbeats: **5109** vs. 10119 — 49.51% reduction - v4.31.0: pass - v4.30.0: pass - v4.29.0: pass - Statement check: byte-identical  Key changes include removing an unused cardinality derivation, sharing the predecessor dimension, and expressing the success predicate through `jointProximityNat`.  A recurrence-first rewrite compiled but increased heartbeats to 5532, so I retained the cheaper split-first form. Plain `rw` under probability binders also failed due to semireducible matching, requiring targeted `simp_rw`.\n\n### 20260821T203211Z-interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 full\nI’ll first read the required arena notes and inspect the existing declaration, then I’ll iterate within the eight-check budget and stop at the first all-version result that improves both metrics.\nThe proof’s main cost appears concentrated in the inductive successor case: it builds several definitional aliases and separately converts the same probability/cardinality fact. I’m checking the surrounding helper signatures and other corpus versions so the rewrite can reuse stable APIs instead of adding automation.\nThe first candidate removes an entire unused cardinality-conversion block and replaces the hand-proved `Fin.snoc` reconstruction with the stable `Fin.snoc_init_self` lemma. I’ve kept the probability comparison explicit and lemma-directed; I’m compiling this candidate now.\nThe second check reached the final lifting step, but the aliases for the two interleaved words obscured instance/type inference and made elaboration more expensive. I’m replacing only that tail with the original explicit type shape while retaining the large verified simplifications earlier in the proof.\nThe newest toolchain now passes at 938 tokens and 8,194 heartbeats, improving both targets. Per the requested loop, I’m moving directly to the all-version check; if all three pass with these positive reductions, I’ll stop.\nRefactored the proof to:  - Remove an unused probability-to-cardinality conversion. - Replace manual `Fin.snoc` reconstruction with `Fin.snoc_init_self`. - Simplify the inductive probability and lifting steps.  Results:  - Length: **938 vs 1353** — **30.67% reduction** - Heartbeats: **8194 vs 10119** — **19.02% reduction** - Passing: **Lean 4.31.0, 4.30.0, and 4.29.0**  Attempts that failed:  - Interleaved-word aliases caused overloaded-notation and instance-inference failures. - Direct `rw` for the singleton probability and direct simplification with `Fin.snoc_init_self` did not match the required expressions.\n\n### 20260821T221955Z-interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 fast\n1 full\nI’ll inspect the existing proof and nearby corpus lemmas, then benchmark a small set of distinct proof shapes while preserving the best-scoring candidate. I’ll keep the statement and all preceding context untouched.\nThe proof’s main cost is not mathematical: it repeatedly re-establishes bookkeeping identities and names intermediate facts that can be passed directly to the existing tensor-gap lemmas. I’m testing a compact induction that keeps those stable lemmas explicit but removes most of that scaffolding.\nThe compact proof has already reduced the measured body from 1,353 to roughly 530 tokens. One attempted generic `Fin.snoc` simplification did not match the project’s dependent-function form; I replaced it with the exact typed identity, and the checker is still elaborating that candidate—an indication this version may be too expensive even if it succeeds.\nThe typed `Fin.snoc` repair is correct in isolation, but the aggressively inlined candidate makes elaboration exceed two minutes, so its apparent heartbeat advantage is unusable. I’m reverting to the stable upstream proof shape and applying smaller, measurable reductions to it; this preserves a compiling incumbent and avoids spending checks on an elaboration cliff.\nThe first stable candidate compiles at 1,192 tokens and 9,021 heartbeats, improving both metrics. The largest confirmed win was deleting an entirely unused probability-to-cardinality conversion. I’ll now test two further independent simplifications, starting with direct composition of the final gap lemmas.\nThe direct probability-monotonicity proof is a substantial improvement: the incumbent is now 866 tokens and 7,085 heartbeats. I’m using the final fast-check slot to inline the one remaining single-use inductive-agreement fact; if it is worse or fails, I’ll restore the 866/7,085 incumbent before compatibility testing.\nThe final inlining attempt hit the same elaboration cliff and was discarded. The checked 866-token / 7,085-heartbeat incumbent has been restored and the experimental commented code removed; I’m now running the required three-toolchain compatibility check.\nRefactored the proof in [interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps.lean](/Users/evanwang/Lean_Refactor/competition/projects/v4.31/Arena/interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps.lean).  - Removed an unused probability-to-cardinality derivation and dead aliases. - Composed the final gap lemmas directly. - Simplified probability monotonicity and the zero case. - Length: **866 vs 1,353** tokens — **35.99% reduction** - Heartbeats: **7,085 vs 10,119** — **29.98% reduction** - Objective sum: **65.97%** - Statement remains byte-identical.  Passing toolchains:  - v4.31.0: 7,085 heartbeats - v4.30.0: 7,146 heartbeats - v4.29.0: 7,876 heartbeats  An aggressively compact rewrite using a generic `Fin.snoc_init_self`, and later fully inlining the inductive-agreement fact, caused elaboration timeouts. Both were discarded.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
