on at most four 80 GB A100 GPUs. Submissions also require JSONL proofs, reproducible harness/inference code, and a short OpenReview technical report covering approach, models, budget accounting, and reproduction. See [`competition-README.md`](competition-README.md), [`app.py`](app.py), and [`contribution.md`](contribution.md) for the retained source text.\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-1-# Lean Refactor Arena — scoring strategy playbook\nSTRATEGY.md-2-\nSTRATEGY.md:3:Working notes on how to maximize the three-part score (length ↓, heartbeats ↓,\nSTRATEGY.md-4-cross-version survival ↑) under the arena's validity rules. Grounded in what\nSTRATEGY.md-5-Lean maintainers say on Zulip. Nothing here is settled; treat it as a hypothesis\nSTRATEGY.md-6-set to test against `benchmark_versions`.\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-15-- **Heartbeats and robustness are the same thing causally.** A proof that only\nSTRATEGY.md-16-  survives via a raised `maxHeartbeats` is running at the search-budget cliff;\nSTRATEGY.md-17-  any version that makes search slightly heavier tips it over. Low search ⇒ low\nSTRATEGY.md:18:  heartbeats ⇒ far from the cliff ⇒ survives version sweeps. A term-mode `exact`\nSTRATEGY.md-19-  has ~zero search, so it is simultaneously shortest, cheapest, and most\nSTRATEGY.md-20-  durable. (Kim Morrison's Tau Ceti rule: no `set_option maxHeartbeats`\nSTRATEGY.md:21:  anywhere. Alex Meiburg's CStar example worked only at 2× heartbeats → broke on\nSTRATEGY.md-22-  a bump.)\nSTRATEGY.md-23-- **Term mode is measurably faster, not just shorter.** Buzzard measured the\nSTRATEGY.md-24-  same lemma at 168 ms (tactic) vs 31 ms (term golf). Mario: \"all other things\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-76-\nSTRATEGY.md-77-**Submission shape (Space clarification):** the row is the benchmark statement\nSTRATEGY.md-78-plus a proof — **nothing else**. Forbidden at upload: `sorry`/`admit`/`axiom`,\nSTRATEGY.md:79:kernel bypasses, `#count_heartbeats`, and **auxiliary top-level declarations /\nSTRATEGY.md-80-syntax extensions** (`def`, `instance`, `attribute`, `macro`, `notation`, …).\nSTRATEGY.md-81-Do not outsource into helper `theorem`/`lemma`s either; treat multi-decl\nSTRATEGY.md-82-submissions as invalid. Heartbeat refs exist for all 15 problems.\nSTRATEGY.md-83-\nSTRATEGY.md:84:### Tier 1 — free tokens (also cut heartbeats, also version-robust)\nSTRATEGY.md-85-\nSTRATEGY.md-86-- Drop the wrapper: `by exact t` → `t`, `by rfl` → `rfl`.\nSTRATEGY.md-87-- Anonymous constructor: `⟨rfl, rfl⟩`, `⟨⟩` for one-constructor goals\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-99-\nSTRATEGY.md-100-### Tier 2 — big single-token collapses (trade against the other two axes)\nSTRATEGY.md-101-\nSTRATEGY.md:102:Use only if you don't also need the heartbeat/robustness thirds. Ranking:\nSTRATEGY.md-103-`omega` is safest (algorithmic, deterministic, version-stable — just weak on\nSTRATEGY.md-104-`Fin` coercions); bare `simp`/`grind` give the largest collapses but are the\nSTRATEGY.md:105:most fragile and heartbeat-heavy.\nSTRATEGY.md-106-\nSTRATEGY.md-107-**Trap:** full term-mode over-golf forces type ascriptions (Lean can't infer\nSTRATEGY.md-108-enough). Ascribe only the outermost layer (Kenny Lau), or use\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-110-\nSTRATEGY.md-111-## Metric 2 — Heartbeats (`avg_hb_pct`)\nSTRATEGY.md-112-\nSTRATEGY.md:113:**Measure right:** `count_heartbeats in <decl>` is a counter delta — raising\nSTRATEGY.md-114-`maxHeartbeats` does **not** lower it. \"It compiles now because I bumped the\nSTRATEGY.md-115-limit\" scores zero here. Use `set_option profiler true` + sorry-bisection to\nSTRATEGY.md-116-find the hot block.\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-130-   for the elaborator is costly); watch instance diamonds (`synthInstance` cost).\nSTRATEGY.md-131-\nSTRATEGY.md-132-**Validity trap:** `native_decide` is the fastest but adds a compiler-trust\nSTRATEGY.md:133:axiom that fails any axiom check. Banned (see below).\nSTRATEGY.md-134-\nSTRATEGY.md-135-## Metric 3 — Robustness (`survival_rate` across `benchmark_versions`)\nSTRATEGY.md-136-\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-156-  behavior; explicit binders are durable.\nSTRATEGY.md-157-\nSTRATEGY.md-158-**Prefer:** term-mode `exact <fully-applied term>`, `rfl`/`decide`/`trivial`\nSTRATEGY.md:159:(kernel-checked), ancient stable names, terminal automation only (let\nSTRATEGY.md-160-`simp`/`omega` *close* the goal so nothing depends on its output shape). For\nSTRATEGY.md-161-forward-durability the community is betting on `grind`/`omega` over\nSTRATEGY.md-162-`aesop`/`nlinarith`, but `grind` is itself churning fast — for surviving\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-213-\nSTRATEGY.md-214-### Bucket B — soundness / kernel-bypass escape hatches (fake proofs, native-vs-kernel divergence)\nSTRATEGY.md-215-\nSTRATEGY.md:216:- **`unsafe`** — marks definitions that skip soundness/termination checks\nSTRATEGY.md-217-  (`unsafeCast` to coerce any type to any type, unrestricted recursion), from\nSTRATEGY.md-218-  which you can manufacture a term of `False` or any goal. A direct route to a\nSTRATEGY.md-219-  fake proof.\nSTRATEGY.md-220-- **`@[extern \"sym\"]` / `extern`** — replaces a function's runtime implementation\nSTRATEGY.md-221-  with an external C symbol; compiled behavior can differ from the Lean\nSTRATEGY.md:222:  definition the kernel checks. The classic \"trust the compiler\" hole — same\nSTRATEGY.md-223-  axiom-scheme risk as `native_decide`, at the definition level.\nSTRATEGY.md-224-- **`@[implemented_by f]`** — same divergence, substitute is another Lean def:\nSTRATEGY.md-225-  the declaration is `X` while `#eval`/`native_decide` run it as `Y`. Lets native\nSTRATEGY.md-226-  evaluation and the kernel disagree — the mechanism behind the \"2+2=5\" example.\nSTRATEGY.md-227-\nSTRATEGY.md:228:**Unifying rule:** no running code the kernel didn't check, and no making the\nSTRATEGY.md-229-compiled world lie to the kernel. It's the definition-level generalization of the\nSTRATEGY.md-230-`native_decide` ban — which strongly implies the full harness also does a\nSTRATEGY.md:231:`#print axioms`-style axiom-clean check. Assume the Oct 1 full benchmark checks\nSTRATEGY.md-232-axioms.\nSTRATEGY.md-233-\nSTRATEGY.md-234-**Practical consequence:** because Bucket B is closed, `decide` is a\nSTRATEGY.md-235-kernel-reduced finisher with no `native_decide` escape — so any goal with\nSTRATEGY.md:236:nontrivial computation is heartbeat-expensive or times out. That pushes even\nSTRATEGY.md-237-decidable goals back toward explicit term/`omega` proofs.\nSTRATEGY.md-238-\nSTRATEGY.md-239-## What the local rig actually measures (Aug 17)\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-249-  is per-thread, so with Lean's parallel elaboration on, the same proof reports\nSTRATEGY.md-250-  774 instead of 111474. Every measurement runs under `Elab.async false`.\nSTRATEGY.md-251-- **Our numbers run a few percent above published** (typically +0.2% to +3%,\nSTRATEGY.md:252:  worst case +18% on the 1.4k-heartbeat CSLib problem, where a constant\nSTRATEGY.md-253-  environment-setup cost dominates). The offset is systematic, so reductions are\nSTRATEGY.md-254-  scored against the locally-measured reference, not the published one.\nSTRATEGY.md-255-- **Reference survival is 100%** where the environment exists: every reference\n--\nSTRATEGY.md-257-  candidate's `compat` is the candidate's fault, not the rig's.\nSTRATEGY.md-258-\nSTRATEGY.md-259-Practical consequence for golfing: the cheapest reliable feedback loop is\nSTRATEGY.md:260:`arena.py check` on the newest toolchain (seconds to ~1 min), with\nSTRATEGY.md-261-`--all-versions` reserved for confirming a candidate that already looks good.\nSTRATEGY.md-262-\nSTRATEGY.md-263-## Pointers\n\n### Current hashes to confirm forbidden wrapper files untouched\nbc0fa49a556e5ad02bbcb590e223e6ebe266af0d9effacbf034b31b1e0d980df  prompts/refactor.md\nbb4f2d0d797ff7c0ce11654978ac2a1ede5b73941612a20f8bf31f89593d7a07  arena.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' harvest_traces.py\njq -r 'select(.name==\\\"fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'\\\\''\\\") | [.timestamp,(.wrapper//\\\"v1-docs-mcp\\\"),.after.length_reduction_pct,.after.heartbeat_reduction_pct,((.after.length_reduction_pct+.after.heartbeat_reduction_pct)*100|round/100),.codex.wall_seconds] | @tsv' runs/episodes.jsonl\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nnames={\\\"Cslib.SKI.parallelReduction_diamond\\\",\\\"CallElimCorrect.extractedOldExprInVars\\\",\\\"Core.InitsUpdatesComm\\\",\\\"fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'\\\",\\\"interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps\\\"}\ngroups=defaultdict(list)\nfor line in open('runs/episodes.jsonl'):\n    r=json.loads(line)\n    if r['name'] not in names: continue\n    w=r.get('wrapper') or 'v1-docs-mcp'\n    a=r['after']\n    groups[w].append((a['length_reduction_pct']+a['heartbeat_reduction_pct'], r['codex']['wall_seconds']))\nfor w,vals in groups.items():\n    print(w, 'n=',len(vals),'mean_sum=',round(sum(x for x,_ in vals)/len(vals),2),'mean_wall_min=',round(sum(t for _,t in vals)/60,2),'total_min=',round(sum(t for _,t in vals)/60,2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' harvest_traces.py\njq -r 'select(.name==\\\"fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'\\\\''\\\") | [.timestamp,(.wrapper//\\\"v1-docs-mcp\\\"),.after.length_reduction_pct,.after.heartbeat_reduction_pct,((.after.length_reduction_pct+.after.heartbeat_reduction_pct)*100|round/100),.codex.wall_seconds] | @tsv' runs/episodes.jsonl\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nnames={\\\"Cslib.SKI.parallelReduction_diamond\\\",\\\"CallElimCorrect.extractedOldExprInVars\\\",\\\"Core.InitsUpdatesComm\\\",\\\"fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'\\\",\\\"interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps\\\"}\ngroups=defaultdict(list)\nfor line in open('runs/episodes.jsonl'):\n    r=json.loads(line)\n    if r['name'] not in names: continue\n    w=r.get('wrapper') or 'v1-docs-mcp'\n    a=r['after']\n    groups[w].append((a['length_reduction_pct']+a['heartbeat_reduction_pct'], r['codex']['wall_seconds']))\nfor w,vals in groups.items():\n    print(w, 'n=',len(vals),'mean_sum=',round(sum(x for x,_ in vals)/len(vals),2),'mean_wall_min=',round(sum(t for _,t in vals)/60,2),'total_min=',round(sum(t for _,t in vals)/60,2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Collect Codex rollouts for recorded episodes into `traces/`.\n\nRaw rollouts are copied verbatim (`traces/raw/`) and a distilled view is\nwritten alongside (`traces/distilled/`) holding just the turn-by-turn\nprompt / reasoning / tool-call / result sequence plus the episode's score, which\nis the part that is useful as training data.\n\n  python3 harvest_traces.py            # every episode in runs/episodes.jsonl\n  python3 harvest_traces.py --name N    # one problem\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport shutil\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Iterator, Optional\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nEPISODES = ROOT / \"runs\" / \"episodes.jsonl\"\nSESSIONS = Path.home() / \".codex\" / \"sessions\"\nTRACES = ROOT / \"traces\"\n\nTRUNC = 4000\n\n\ndef episodes(name: Optional[str] = None) -> Iterator[dict[str, Any]]:\n    if not EPISODES.exists():\n        return\n    for line in EPISODES.read_text().splitlines():\n        if not line.strip():\n            continue\n        rec = json.loads(line)\n        if name is None or rec.get(\"name\") == name:\n            yield rec\n\n\ndef find_rollout(rec: dict[str, Any]) -> Optional[Path]:\n    codex = rec.get(\"codex\") or {}\n    for key in (\"session_id\", \"thread_id\", \"conversation_id\"):\n        ident = codex.get(key)\n        if ident:\n            hits = list(SESSIONS.rglob(f\"rollout-*{ident}*.jsonl\"))\n            if hits:\n                return hits[0]\n    explicit = codex.get(\"rollout_path\")\n    if explicit:\n        p = Path(explicit)\n        if p.is_file():\n            return p\n    return None\n\n\ndef text_of(content: Any) -> str:\n    if isinstance(content, str):\n        return content\n    if isinstance(content, list):\n        parts = []\n        for chunk in content:\n            if isinstance(chunk, dict):\n                parts.append(chunk.get(\"text\") or chunk.get(\"summary\") or \"\")\n        return \"\\n\".join(p for p in parts if p)\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef distill(rollout: Path) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    items: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for line in rollout.read_text().splitlines():\n        if not line.strip():\n            continue\n        try:\n            event = json.loads(line)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            continue\n        if event.get(\"type\") != \"response_item\":\n            continue\n        payload = event.get(\"payload\") or {}\n        kind = payload.get(\"type\")\n        stamp = event.get(\"timestamp\")\n        if kind == \"message\":\n            body = text_of(payload.get(\"content\"))\n            if body and payload.get(\"role\") != \"developer\":\n                items.append({\"t\": stamp, \"kind\": payload.get(\"role\"), \"text\": body[:TRUNC]})\n        elif kind == \"reasoning\":\n            body = text_of(payload.get(\"summary\") or payload.get(\"content\"))\n            if body:\n                items.append({\"t\": stamp, \"kind\": \"reasoning\", \"text\": body[:TRUNC]})\n        elif kind in (\"function_call\", \"custom_tool_call\", \"local_shell_call\"):\n            items.append({\n                \"t\": stamp,\n                \"kind\": \"tool_call\",\n                \"tool\": payload.get(\"name\") or kind,\n                \"args\": str(payload.get(\"arguments\") or payload.get(\"input\") or \"\")[:TRUNC],\n            })\n        elif kind in (\"function_call_output\", \"custom_tool_call_output\"):\n            items.append({\n                \"t\": stamp,\n                \"kind\": \"tool_result\",\n                \"text\": str(payload.get(\"output\") or \"\")[:TRUNC],\n            })\n    return items\n\n\ndef harvest(name: Optional[str] = None) -> None:\n    (TRACES / \"raw\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (TRACES / \"distilled\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for rec in episodes(name):\n        rollout = find_rollout(rec)\n        if rollout is None:\n            print(f\"no rollout found for {rec['name']} @ {rec.get('timestamp')}\")\n            continue\n        raw_dest = TRACES / \"raw\" / rollout.name\n        shutil.copy2(rollout, raw_dest)\n        items = distill(rollout)\n        stem = f\"{rec.get('timestamp')}-{rec['name'].replace('.', '_')}.jsonl\"\n        dest = TRACES / \"distilled\" / stem\n        after = rec.get(\"after\") or {}\n        with dest.open(\"w\") as fh:\n            fh.write(json.dumps({\n                \"kind\": \"episode\",\n                \"name\": rec[\"name\"],\n                \"model\": (rec.get(\"codex\") or {}).get(\"model\"),\n                \"effort\": (rec.get(\"codex\") or {}).get(\"effort\"),\n                \"wall_seconds\": (rec.get(\"codex\") or {}).get(\"wall_seconds\"),\n                \"compiled\": after.get(\"compiled\"),\n                \"length\": after.get(\"length\"),\n                \"length_reduction_pct\": after.get(\"length_reduction_pct\"),\n                \"heartbeats\": after.get(\"heartbeats\"),\n                \"heartbeat_reduction_pct\": after.get(\"heartbeat_reduction_pct\"),\n                \"compat\": after.get(\"compat\"),\n                \"rollout\": str(rollout),\n            }) + \"\\n\")\n            for item in items:\n                fh.write(json.dumps(item) + \"\\n\")\n        print(f\"{rec['name']}: {len(items)} items → {dest.relative_to(ROOT)}\")\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--name\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    harvest(args.name)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n20260820T230206Z\tv1-docs-mcp\t67.8\t80.5\t148.3\t715.7\n20260821T202628Z\tv2-tight-loop\t71.45\t76.73\t148.18\t339.2\n20260821T221956Z\tv3-official-objective\t65.45\t75.63\t141.08\t401.3\nv1-docs-mcp n= 5 mean_sum= 115.47 mean_wall_min= 61.65 total_min= 61.65\nv2-tight-loop n= 5 mean_sum= 89.46 mean_wall_min= 26.41 total_min= 26.41\nv3-official-objective n= 5 mean_sum= 80.48 mean_wall_min= 41.37 total_min= 41.37\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
